In daedalus/eval/graph_delta.py, replace the current _module_literals with:

```python
def _module_literals(module: str, text: str) -> set:
    import ast
    from collections import Counter
    try:
        tree = ast.parse(text)
    except SyntaxError:
        return set()
    c: Counter = Counter()
    def walk_node(node):
        if isinstance(node, (ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef)):
            return  # function bodies handled by _literals_by_function
        if isinstance(node, (ast.Assign, ast.AnnAssign)):
            for sub in ast.walk(node):
                if isinstance(sub, ast.Constant):
                    r = repr(sub.value)
                    c[r if len(r) <= 80 else r[:79] + '…'] += 1
        for child in ast.iter_child_nodes(node):
            walk_node(child)
    for stmt in tree.body:
        walk_node(stmt)
    return {f"{k}#{i}" for k, n in c.items() for i in range(n)}
```

This captures constants in all module-level contexts (classes, conditionals, loops) while avoiding re-extracting function-local constants.
